course: dictionary
lesson: 11511
title: Airplane: a flying machine
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An airplane is a flying machine with wings and engines. It carries people or goods through the air. In the UK and Australia, people often say aeroplane for the same thing.
explain: «We flew to Spain by airplane.» Here by airplane tells you how the trip was made: through the air, in a flying machine. «Mum got on an airplane at six o'clock.» Get on an airplane means climb aboard the plane to travel.
explain: The word has a second meaning too. «Ava folded a paper airplane and threw it across the room.» A paper airplane is made of paper, so it is a small toy model, not a real plane you could fly in. Always check the clues around the word.
explain: Phrases can change the meaning. «Please switch on airplane mode before we take off.» Airplane mode is a setting on a phone that switches off its signals, as is needed on a flight. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
fact: An airplane is a noun, and its plural is airplanes.
fact: «Airplane» means a flying machine with wings and engines that carries people or goods through the air.
fact: In the UK and Australia, people often say aeroplane for the same thing.
fact: «Paper airplane» means a toy model of a flying machine, made from folded paper.
fact: «By airplane» means travelling in a flying machine.
exercise: «We flew to Spain by airplane.» How did the family travel? | By bus | On foot | *By airplane | By boat
exercise: Mia says aeroplane means something different from airplane. What is the answer? | They are a boat and a plane | They mean a car | *They mean the same flying machine; UK and Australia use aeroplane | They mean a toy only
exercise: «Sam folded a paper airplane and threw it.» What does paper airplane mean? | A real plane with a big engine | A paper bag | A paper cup | *A toy model of a flying machine, made of paper
test: «The airplane landed at noon.» What landed? | A bird | A cloud | *A flying machine | A boat
test: Which word means the same as airplane in the UK and Australia? | aeronaut | *aeroplane | airline | airport
exam: Ella says, «Please switch on airplane mode.» What does airplane mode mean on a phone? | *The phone's signals are switched off, as on a flight | The phone flies away | The phone turns into a toy airplane | The phone takes photos from the sky
